/-!
# The theorem on formal functions for the comparison map of Stacks 088B

Let `f : X ⟶ Y` be a proper morphism onto a Noetherian scheme, let `𝒥 ⊆ 𝒪_Y` be a quasi-coherent
sheaf of ideals, write `ℐ = 𝒥.comap f`, and let `𝓕` be a coherent `𝒪_X`-module. The comparison
morphism of inverse systems

`c : (f_*𝓕)^ ⟶ f_*(𝓕^)`,     `c_n : (f_*𝓕) / 𝒥 ⁿ⁺¹ (f_*𝓕) ⟶ f_*(𝓕 / ℐ ⁿ⁺¹𝓕)`

of `StacksDraft.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.CompletionProper`
`.ExceptionalComparisonMapPushforwardAux` is the map Stacks 088B wants to be an isomorphism on
inverse limits. **This file proves that over an affine Noetherian base**, in the form the
globalisation needs: the induced map on the limits of the modules of global sections is an
isomorphism.

The argument is the one the source gives. Over an affine base `Y = Spec A` with `I = 𝒥(Y)`:

* the sections of the limit of the completion of a coherent module on `Y` over an affine open
  are the `I`-adic completion of its sections there, which is
  `Stacks.Algebraization.completionSectionsEquiv` (Stacks 0880); and
* the limit of the sections of the direct images `Γ(Y, f_*(𝓕 / ℐ ⁿ𝓕)) = Γ(X, 𝓕 / ℐ ⁿ𝓕)` is the
  `I`-adic completion of `Γ(X, 𝓕)`, which is the theorem on formal functions
  [Stacks, Tag 02OC] in degree zero.

Both identifications carry the image of a section to its images under the projections, so the
comparison map is the identity of `Γ(X, 𝓕) ^∧_I` read through the two of them, and therefore an
isomorphism. The passage from "an isomorphism after each identification" to "an isomorphism" is
`Stacks.Coherent.isIso_of_adicCompletion_equiv`, which needs the target to be Hausdorff for the
ideal; this is the source's own argument that a map out of an adic completion is determined by
its values on the image of the module.

What this file does **not** do is descend from the affine case to a general Noetherian base.
`Stacks.Coherent.isIso_limMap_of_isIso_affineSections` reduces `IsIso (limMap c)` to the
sections over each affine open `U ⊆ Y`, and the affine case applies to the restricted data
`f ∣_ U`, `𝒥.comap U.ι`, `𝓕|_(f⁻¹U)`; the identification of the restriction of `c` with the
comparison map of that restricted data is not proved here.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Coherent.towerEquivLimitShift` — the concrete limit of a tower of modules, identified
  with the categorical limit of its index shift.
* `Stacks.Coherent.toSpecGlobalSections` — the structure morphism `X ⟶ Spec Γ(Y, ⊤)` of a scheme
  over an affine base.
* `Stacks.Coherent.rightDerivedZeroSectionsEquiv` — degree-zero cohomology over an affine base,
  identified with global sections as a module over the global functions of the base.
* `Stacks.Coherent.completionTermIso` — the `n`-th term of the completion functor of Stacks 0880,
  identified with the `(n+1)`-st term of the tower of ideal-power quotients.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Coherent.adicCompletion_linearMap_ext` and
  `Stacks.Coherent.isIso_of_adicCompletion_equiv` — a map out of an adic completion is determined
  by its values on the image of the module, and two models of one adic completion are compared by
  checking the comparison there.
* `Stacks.Coherent.isIso_of_isIso_affineSections`, `Stacks.Coherent.map_limMap_eq` and
  `Stacks.Coherent.isIso_limMap_of_isIso_affineSections` — a morphism of sheaves of modules, and
  an induced map on limits of inverse systems of them, is an isomorphism as soon as it is one on
  the sections over every affine open.
* `Stacks.Coherent.baseRingHom_toSpecGlobalSections`,
  `Stacks.Coherent.comap_eq_ofIdealTop` and
  `Stacks.Coherent.baseIdealSheaf_toSpecGlobalSections` — the ring map and the ideal sheaf that
  the theorem on formal functions attaches to an affine base are the ones of `f` and `𝒥.comap f`.
* `Stacks.Coherent.exists_cohomologyTowerEquiv` — [Stacks, Tag 02OC] in degree zero, with the
  inverse-image ideal sheaf substituted for the ideal sheaf generated by the base ideal.
* `Stacks.Coherent.exists_pushforwardCompletionSectionsEquiv` — **the theorem on formal functions
  as a statement about sections**: the `𝒥(Y)`-adic completion of `Γ(Y, f_*𝓕)` is the limit of the
  sections of the direct images of the terms of the completion of `𝓕`.
* `Stacks.Coherent.isIso_limMap_affineSections_of_completionProjection_comp` and
  `Stacks.Coherent.isIso_limMap_affineSections_pushforwardCompletionComparison` — **the
  comparison map of Stacks 088B is an isomorphism on the limits of global sections over an affine
  Noetherian base.**

## Implementation notes

The theorem on formal functions is consumed through
`Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.exists_formalFunctionsEquiv_of_02O8`, whose hypothesis is
discharged by `Stacks.FormalFunctions.isReesFinite_cohomologyIdealPowerSystem`; nothing is
carried. Its conclusion is stated for the concrete limit
`Stacks.IntertwinedFiltration.towerLimit` of the tower `n ↦ Hᵖ(X, 𝓕 / ℐ ⁿ𝓕)`, indexed by the
exponent itself, while the completion functor of Stacks 0880 is indexed so that its `n`-th term
is the quotient by `ℐ ⁿ⁺¹`. The two gaps are bridged once and for all by
`Stacks.Coherent.towerEquivLimitShift`, which compares a tower with the categorical limit of its
index shift, and by `Stacks.Coherent.completionTermIso`. The transitivity hypothesis of that
comparison is needed because `Stacks.IntertwinedFiltration.towerLimit` assumes nothing about the
composites of the transition maps; for the tower of cohomology modules it is
`Stacks.Coherent.idealPowerQuotientDrop_comp`.

`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules` is a `def` for `SheafOfModules X.ringCatSheaf`, and a goal
mentioning both presentations is not type-correct at the transparency a rewrite motive is built
at, so `rw` cannot fire on it even with a lemma written for it. Every such step below is done in
term mode out of `CategoryTheory.Category.assoc`, `congrArg` and `Eq.trans`, or by `exact` against
a `have` stated at the spelling the goal uses, rather than by relaxing definitional-equality
transparency. The same
device handles `CategoryTheory.Limits.cokernel`, whose definition is not exposed, so that
`idealPowerQuotient I n M` and `(adicQuotientSystem I M).obj (op n)` are interchangeable only up
to unexposed unfolding.

`AdicCompletion.congr` is linear for `AdicCompletion I A`, not for `A`; the transport of the
completion along `Stacks.Coherent.rightDerivedZeroSectionsEquiv` therefore goes through
`LinearEquiv.restrictScalars`. Its computation on the image of an element is `rfl`, since both
`AdicCompletion.congr_symm_apply` and `AdicCompletion.map_of` are.

`Stacks.Algebraization.affineSectionFunctor U` composed with
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.pushforward f` is definitionally the global sections of `X`
with scalars restricted along `f.appTop`, which is what makes
`Stacks.Coherent.rightDerivedZeroSectionsEquiv` a map into the sections of a direct image with no
transport; only the equality of the two ring maps, which is
`Stacks.Coherent.baseRingHom_toSpecGlobalSections`, has to be proved.

No Stacks attribute is attached: the tags 02OB and 02OC are registered elsewhere, and
the statement proved here is the affine case of the comparison of Stacks 088B rather than that
tag's own claim.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 088B](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/088B)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02OC](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02OC)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02O8](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02O8)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0880](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0880)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite TopologicalSpace
open scoped AlgebraicGeometry

universe u

namespace Stacks.Coherent

/-! ### The concrete limit of a tower is the categorical limit of its index shift -/

section TowerLimit

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {P : ℕ → Type u}
  [∀ n, AddCommGroup (P n)] [∀ n, Module A (P n)]
  {T : ∀ m n : ℕ, m ≤ n → P n →ₗ[A] P m} {E : ℕᵒᵖ ⥤ ModuleCat.{u} A}
  {θ : ∀ n : ℕ, P (n + 1) ≃ₗ[A] E.obj (op n)}

/-- The transitivity hypothesis on the transition maps of a tower: it is a functor, not merely a
family of maps. -/
public abbrev IsTowerTransitive {P : ℕ → Type u} [∀ n, AddCommGroup (P n)]
    [∀ n, Module A (P n)] (T : ∀ m n : ℕ, m ≤ n → P n →ₗ[A] P m) : Prop :=
  ∀ (m n k : ℕ) (h : m ≤ n) (h' : n ≤ k) (x : P k), T m n h (T n k h' x) = T m k (h.trans h') x

/-- The compatibility hypothesis of `Stacks.Coherent.towerEquivLimitShift`: the comparison maps
intertwine the transitions of the tower with those of the shifted inverse system. -/
public abbrev IsShiftCompatible {P : ℕ → Type u} [∀ n, AddCommGroup (P n)]
    [∀ n, Module A (P n)] (T : ∀ m n : ℕ, m ≤ n → P n →ₗ[A] P m) (E : ℕᵒᵖ ⥤ ModuleCat.{u} A)
    (θ : ∀ n : ℕ, P (n + 1) ≃ₗ[A] E.obj (op n)) : Prop :=
  ∀ (m n : ℕ) (h : m ≤ n) (x : P (n + 1)),
    (E.map (homOfLE h).op).hom (θ n x) =
      θ m (T (m + 1) (n + 1) (Nat.add_le_add_right h 1) x)

/-- The concrete limit of the tower, as a cone over the shifted inverse system. -/
public def shiftedTowerCone (hθ : IsShiftCompatible T E θ) : Cone E where
  pt := ModuleCat.of A (Stacks.IntertwinedFiltration.towerLimit P T)
  π :=
    { app n := ModuleCat.ofHom
        ((θ n.unop).toLinearMap ∘ₗ Stacks.IntertwinedFiltration.towerLimit.proj (n.unop + 1))
      naturality i j a := by
        refine (Category.id_comp _).trans (ModuleCat.hom_ext (LinearMap.ext fun x => ?_))
        have h : j.unop ≤ i.unop := leOfHom a.unop
        have ha : a = (homOfLE h).op := Subsingleton.elim _ _
        change θ j.unop ((x : ∀ k, P k) (j.unop + 1)) =
          (E.map a).hom (θ i.unop ((x : ∀ k, P k) (i.unop + 1)))
        rw [ha, hθ j.unop i.unop h]
        exact congrArg (θ j.unop)
          (Stacks.IntertwinedFiltration.towerLimit_compat x (j.unop + 1) (i.unop + 1)
            (Nat.add_le_add_right h 1)).symm }

/-- The map from the limit of the shifted inverse system to the concrete limit of the tower. -/
public def limitToShiftedTower (hT : IsTowerTransitive T) (hθ : IsShiftCompatible T E θ) :
    (limit E : ModuleCat.{u} A) →ₗ[A] Stacks.IntertwinedFiltration.towerLimit P T :=
  LinearMap.codRestrict _
      (LinearMap.pi fun n => (T n (n + 1) (Nat.le_succ n)).comp
        ((θ n).symm.toLinearMap.comp (limit.π E (op n)).hom)) <| by
    intro x m n h
    have hw : (E.map (homOfLE h).op).hom ((limit.π E (op n)).hom x) =
        (limit.π E (op m)).hom x :=
      congrArg (fun k : limit E ⟶ E.obj (op m) => k.hom x) (limit.w E (homOfLE h).op)
    have hy : (θ m).symm ((limit.π E (op m)).hom x) =
        T (m + 1) (n + 1) (Nat.add_le_add_right h 1)
          ((θ n).symm ((limit.π E (op n)).hom x)) := by
      have h1 := hθ m n h ((θ n).symm ((limit.π E (op n)).hom x))
      rw [(θ n).apply_symm_apply, hw] at h1
      rw [h1, (θ m).symm_apply_apply]
    change T m n h (T n (n + 1) (Nat.le_succ n) ((θ n).symm ((limit.π E (op n)).hom x))) =
      T m (m + 1) (Nat.le_succ m) ((θ m).symm ((limit.π E (op m)).hom x))
    rw [hT m n (n + 1) h (Nat.le_succ n), hy,
      hT m (m + 1) (n + 1) (Nat.le_succ m) (Nat.add_le_add_right h 1)]

/-- **The concrete limit of a tower of modules is the categorical limit of its index shift.** -/
public def towerEquivLimitShift (hT : IsTowerTransitive T) (hθ : IsShiftCompatible T E θ) :
    Stacks.IntertwinedFiltration.towerLimit P T ≃ₗ[A] (limit E : ModuleCat.{u} A) where
  toFun := (limit.lift E (shiftedTowerCone hθ)).hom
  map_add' := map_add _
  map_smul' := map_smul _
  invFun := limitToShiftedTower hT hθ
  left_inv y := by
    refine Stacks.IntertwinedFiltration.towerLimit_ext fun n => ?_
    have hπ : (limit.π E (op n)).hom ((limit.lift E (shiftedTowerCone hθ)).hom y) =
        θ n (Stacks.IntertwinedFiltration.towerLimit.proj (n + 1) y) :=
      congrArg (fun k : (shiftedTowerCone hθ).pt ⟶ E.obj (op n) => k.hom y)
        (limit.lift_π (shiftedTowerCone hθ) (op n))
    change T n (n + 1) (Nat.le_succ n)
        ((θ n).symm ((limit.π E (op n)).hom ((limit.lift E (shiftedTowerCone hθ)).hom y))) =
      (y : ∀ k, P k) n
    rw [hπ, (θ n).symm_apply_apply]
    exact Stacks.IntertwinedFiltration.towerLimit_compat y n (n + 1) (Nat.le_succ n)
  right_inv x := by
    refine Concrete.limit_ext E _ _ fun n => ?_
    have hπ : (limit.π E n).hom
          ((limit.lift E (shiftedTowerCone hθ)).hom (limitToShiftedTower hT hθ x)) =
        ((shiftedTowerCone hθ).π.app n).hom (limitToShiftedTower hT hθ x) :=
      congrArg (fun k : (shiftedTowerCone hθ).pt ⟶ E.obj n =>
        k.hom (limitToShiftedTower hT hθ x)) (limit.lift_π (shiftedTowerCone hθ) n)
    refine hπ.trans ?_
    change θ n.unop (T (n.unop + 1) (n.unop + 1 + 1) (Nat.le_succ (n.unop + 1))
        ((θ (n.unop + 1)).symm ((limit.π E (op (n.unop + 1))).hom x))) = (limit.π E n).hom x
    have h1 := hθ n.unop (n.unop + 1) (Nat.le_succ n.unop)
      ((θ (n.unop + 1)).symm ((limit.π E (op (n.unop + 1))).hom x))
    rw [(θ (n.unop + 1)).apply_symm_apply] at h1
    refine h1.symm.trans ?_
    exact congrArg (fun k : limit E ⟶ E.obj (op n.unop) => k.hom x)
      (limit.w E (homOfLE (Nat.le_succ n.unop)).op)

/-- The components of `Stacks.Coherent.towerEquivLimitShift`. -/
public lemma limit_π_towerEquivLimitShift (hT : IsTowerTransitive T)
    (hθ : IsShiftCompatible T E θ) (n : ℕ)
    (y : Stacks.IntertwinedFiltration.towerLimit P T) :
    (limit.π E (op n)).hom (towerEquivLimitShift hT hθ y) =
      θ n (Stacks.IntertwinedFiltration.towerLimit.proj (n + 1) y) :=
  congrArg (fun k : (shiftedTowerCone hθ).pt ⟶ E.obj (op n) => k.hom y)
    (limit.lift_π (shiftedTowerCone hθ) (op n))

end TowerLimit

/-! ### Two facts about adic completions -/

/-- **A map out of an adic completion is determined by its values on the image of the module**,
when the target is Hausdorff for the ideal and the ideal is finitely generated. -/
public lemma adicCompletion_linearMap_ext
    {A M N : Type*} [CommRing A] (I : Ideal A) (hI : I.FG)
    [AddCommGroup M] [Module A M] [AddCommGroup N] [Module A N]
    [IsHausdorff I N] {f g : AdicCompletion I M →ₗ[A] N}
    (h : ∀ x : M, f (AdicCompletion.of I M x) = g (AdicCompletion.of I M x)) : f = g := by
  refine LinearMap.ext fun x => sub_eq_zero.mp (IsHausdorff.haus' (I := I) _ fun n => ?_)
  rw [SModEq.sub_mem, sub_zero]
  obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := (I ^ n • (⊤ : Submodule A M)).mkQ_surjective
    (AdicCompletion.eval I M n x)
  have hx : x - AdicCompletion.of I M y ∈
      I ^ n • (⊤ : Submodule A (AdicCompletion I M)) := by
    rw [AdicCompletion.pow_smul_top_eq_ker_eval hI, LinearMap.mem_ker,
      map_sub, AdicCompletion.eval_of, hy, sub_self]
  have hl : I ^ n • (⊤ : Submodule A (AdicCompletion I M)) ≤
      (I ^ n • (⊤ : Submodule A N)).comap (f - g) := by
    rw [← Submodule.map_le_iff_le_comap, Submodule.map_smul'']
    gcongr
    exact le_top
  simpa only [Submodule.mem_comap, LinearMap.sub_apply, map_sub, h y, sub_self, sub_zero]
    using hl hx

/-- **A morphism between two models of one adic completion is an isomorphism** as soon as it
matches the two identifications on the image of the module. -/
public lemma isIso_of_adicCompletion_equiv
    {A M : Type u} [CommRing A] (I : Ideal A) (hI : I.FG)
    [AddCommGroup M] [Module A M] {N P : ModuleCat.{u} A}
    (eN : AdicCompletion I M ≃ₗ[A] N) (eP : AdicCompletion I M ≃ₗ[A] P)
    (a : N ⟶ P)
    (ha : ∀ x : M, a.hom (eN (AdicCompletion.of I M x)) = eP (AdicCompletion.of I M x)) :
    IsIso a := by
  let : IsAdicComplete I (AdicCompletion I M) := AdicCompletion.isAdicComplete hI
  have he : eP.symm.toLinearMap.comp (a.hom.comp eN.toLinearMap) = LinearMap.id := by
    refine adicCompletion_linearMap_ext I hI fun x => ?_
    simpa using congrArg eP.symm (ha x)
  have heq : a = (eN.symm.trans eP).toModuleIso.hom := by
    refine ModuleCat.hom_ext (LinearMap.ext fun y => eP.symm.injective ?_)
    simpa using LinearMap.congr_fun he (eN.symm y)
  rw [heq]
  infer_instance

/-! ### Limits, sections and isomorphisms of sheaves of modules -/

/-- A functor preserving two limits carries the induced map on limits to the induced map on the
limits of the composites. -/
public lemma map_limMap_eq
    {C D E : Type*} [Category C] [Category D] [Category E]
    (S : D ⥤ E) {F G : C ⥤ D} [HasLimit F] [HasLimit G]
    [PreservesLimit F S] [PreservesLimit G S] (a : F ⟶ G) :
    S.map (limMap a) = (preservesLimitIso S F).hom ≫
      limMap (Functor.whiskerRight a S) ≫ (preservesLimitIso S G).inv := by
  apply (cancel_mono (preservesLimitIso S G).hom).mp
  simp only [Category.assoc, Iso.inv_hom_id, Category.comp_id]
  apply limit.hom_ext
  intro n
  simp only [Category.assoc, preservesLimitIso_hom_π, limMap_π,
    Functor.whiskerRight_app, preservesLimitIso_hom_π_assoc, ← Functor.map_comp]

/-- **A morphism of sheaves of modules on a scheme is an isomorphism as soon as it is one on the
sections over every affine open**, the affine opens forming a basis of the topology. -/
public lemma isIso_of_isIso_affineSections {X : Scheme.{u}} {M N : X.Modules}
    (a : M ⟶ N) (ha : ∀ U : X.affineOpens, IsIso (a.val.app (op U.1))) :
    IsIso a := by
  have hb : Opens.IsBasis (Set.range (fun A : X.affineOpens => A.1)) := by
    have heq : Set.range (fun A : X.affineOpens => A.1) = X.affineOpens := by
      ext W
      exact ⟨by rintro ⟨A, rfl⟩; exact A.property, fun hW => ⟨⟨W, hW⟩, rfl⟩⟩
    rw [heq]
    exact X.isBasis_affineOpens
  have hp : IsIso ((SheafOfModules.toSheaf X.ringCatSheaf).map a) := by
    apply TopCat.Sheaf.isIso_iff_isIso_basis hb
    intro A
    rw [ConcreteCategory.isIso_iff_bijective]
    have hA := ha A
    rw [ConcreteCategory.isIso_iff_bijective] at hA
    exact hA
  apply (Scheme.Modules.Hom.isIso_iff_isIso_app).mpr
  intro W
  have hT : IsIso ((SheafOfModules.toSheaf X.ringCatSheaf).map a).hom := by
    have := hp
    infer_instance
  exact (NatTrans.isIso_iff_isIso_app
    ((SheafOfModules.toSheaf X.ringCatSheaf).map a).hom).mp hT (op W)

/-- **The induced map on limits of two inverse systems of sheaves of modules is an isomorphism as
soon as it is one on the limits of the sections over every affine open.** -/
public lemma isIso_limMap_of_isIso_affineSections {X : Scheme.{u}}
    {G H : ℕᵒᵖ ⥤ X.Modules} (a : G ⟶ H)
    (ha : ∀ U : X.affineOpens,
      IsIso (limMap (Functor.whiskerRight a
        (Stacks.Algebraization.affineSectionFunctor U)))) : IsIso (limMap a) := by
  refine isIso_of_isIso_affineSections _ fun U => ?_
  let : PreservesLimit G (Stacks.Algebraization.affineSectionFunctor U) :=
    Stacks.Algebraization.affineSectionFunctor_preservesLimit U G
  let : PreservesLimit H (Stacks.Algebraization.affineSectionFunctor U) :=
    Stacks.Algebraization.affineSectionFunctor_preservesLimit U H
  have hmap : IsIso ((Stacks.Algebraization.affineSectionFunctor U).map (limMap a)) := by
    rw [map_limMap_eq]
    let := ha U
    infer_instance
  rw [ConcreteCategory.isIso_iff_bijective]
  rw [ConcreteCategory.isIso_iff_bijective] at hmap
  exact hmap

/-! ### The structure morphism to the spectrum of the global functions -/

/-- The structure morphism of `X` over an affine base `Y`, read as a morphism to the spectrum of
the ring of global functions of `Y`. -/
@[ega "II 5.1.2" "more general"]
public def toSpecGlobalSections {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Y) :
    X ⟶ Spec (.of Γ(Y, ⊤)) :=
  f ≫ Y.toSpecΓ

/-- A proper morphism to an affine base stays proper after composing with the identification of
the base with the spectrum of its global functions. -/
public lemma isProper_toSpecGlobalSections {X Y : Scheme.{u}} [IsAffine Y] (f : X ⟶ Y)
    [IsProper f] : IsProper (toSpecGlobalSections f) := by
  let : IsIso Y.toSpecΓ := IsAffine.affine
  exact inferInstanceAs (IsProper (f ≫ Y.toSpecΓ))

/-- The ring map through which the global functions of the base act is the map on global
functions of `f` itself. -/
public lemma baseRingHom_toSpecGlobalSections {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Y) :
    Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.baseRingHom Γ(Y, ⊤) (toSpecGlobalSections f) =
      f.appTop.hom := by
  change ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of Γ(Y, ⊤))).inv ≫ (f ≫ Y.toSpecΓ).appTop).hom = _
  rw [Scheme.Hom.comp_appTop, Scheme.toSpecΓ_appTop, ← Category.assoc]
  change ((((Scheme.ΓSpecIso Γ(Y, ⊤)).inv ≫ (Scheme.ΓSpecIso Γ(Y, ⊤)).hom) ≫
    f.appTop) : Γ(Y, ⊤) ⟶ Γ(X, ⊤)).hom = _
  rw [Iso.inv_hom_id, Category.id_comp]

/-- Over an affine base the inverse-image ideal sheaf is the ideal sheaf generated by the image
of the global ideal. -/
public lemma comap_eq_ofIdealTop {X Y : Scheme.{u}} [IsAffine Y]
    (f : X ⟶ Y) (J : Y.IdealSheafData) :
    J.comap f = Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop
      (Ideal.map f.appTop.hom (J.ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top Y⟩)) := by
  refine Scheme.IdealSheafData.ext (funext fun U => ?_)
  rw [Stacks.IdealSheaf.ideal_comap_appLE J f ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top Y⟩ U (by simp),
    Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop_ideal, Ideal.map_map]
  congr 1

/-- The ideal sheaf that the theorem on formal functions attaches to the global ideal of an
affine base is the inverse-image ideal sheaf. -/
public lemma baseIdealSheaf_toSpecGlobalSections {X Y : Scheme.{u}} [IsAffine Y]
    (f : X ⟶ Y) (J : Y.IdealSheafData) :
    Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.baseIdealSheaf Γ(Y, ⊤)
        (J.ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top Y⟩) (toSpecGlobalSections f) = J.comap f := by
  rw [comap_eq_ofIdealTop f J]
  exact congrArg Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop
    (congrArg (fun φ => Ideal.map φ (J.ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top Y⟩))
      (baseRingHom_toSpecGlobalSections f))

/-- **Degree-zero cohomology over an affine base is global sections.** The `A`-module structures
match because the ring map of the structure morphism to `Spec Γ(Y, ⊤)` is the map on global
functions of `f`. -/
public def rightDerivedZeroSectionsEquiv {X Y : Scheme.{u}} [IsAffine Y] (f : X ⟶ Y)
    (N : X.Modules) :
    Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.cohomologyOverBase (Γ(Y, ⊤) : Type u)
        (toSpecGlobalSections f) 0 N ≃ₗ[Γ(Y, ⊤)]
      (Stacks.Algebraization.affineSectionFunctor (⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top Y⟩ : Y.affineOpens)).obj
        ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).obj N) :=
  letI e := ((Functor.rightDerivedZeroIsoSelf
    (Stacks.Cohomology.AffineBase.moduleGlobalSections X)).app N).toLinearEquiv
  { toFun := e
    map_add' := e.map_add
    invFun := e.symm
    left_inv := e.left_inv
    right_inv := e.right_inv
    map_smul' := fun a x => by
      change e (Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.baseRingHom (Γ(Y, ⊤) : Type u)
        (toSpecGlobalSections f) a • x) = _
      rw [baseRingHom_toSpecGlobalSections f]
      exact e.map_smul (f.appTop.hom a) x }

/-- The exponent-lowering maps of the tower of ideal-power quotients compose. -/
public lemma idealPowerQuotientDrop_comp {X : Scheme.{u}} (I : X.IdealSheafData)
    (F : X.Modules) {m n k : ℕ} (h : m ≤ n) (h' : n ≤ k) :
    Stacks.Algebraization.idealPowerQuotientDrop I h' F ≫
        Stacks.Algebraization.idealPowerQuotientDrop I h F =
      Stacks.Algebraization.idealPowerQuotientDrop I (h.trans h') F := by
  have : Epi (cokernel.π (C := X.Modules)
      (Stacks.Algebraization.idealPowerMultiple I k F).ι) :=
    Stacks.Algebraization.epi_cokernel_π_submodule_ι _
  refine (cancel_epi (cokernel.π (C := X.Modules)
    (Stacks.Algebraization.idealPowerMultiple I k F).ι)).1 ?_
  rw [← Category.assoc, Stacks.Algebraization.idealPowerQuotientDrop_π,
    Stacks.Algebraization.idealPowerQuotientDrop_π,
    Stacks.Algebraization.idealPowerQuotientDrop_π]

/-- **The theorem on formal functions in degree zero over an affine base**, in the tower form.
The ideal sheaf of the statement is the inverse-image ideal sheaf, by
`Stacks.Coherent.baseIdealSheaf_toSpecGlobalSections`. -/
public lemma exists_cohomologyTowerEquiv
    {X Y : Scheme.{u}} [IsAffine Y] [IsNoetherian Y] (f : X ⟶ Y) [IsProper f]
    (J : Y.IdealSheafData) (F : X.Modules) [F.IsCoherent] :
    ∃ e : AdicCompletion (J.ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top Y⟩)
          (Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.cohomologyOverBase (Γ(Y, ⊤) : Type u)
            (toSpecGlobalSections f) 0 F) ≃ₗ[Γ(Y, ⊤)]
          Stacks.IntertwinedFiltration.towerLimit
            (fun n => Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.cohomologyOverBase (Γ(Y, ⊤) : Type u)
              (toSpecGlobalSections f) 0
              (Stacks.Algebraization.idealPowerQuotient (J.comap f) n F))
            (fun _ _ h => (Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.cohomologyOverBaseMap
              (Γ(Y, ⊤) : Type u) (toSpecGlobalSections f) 0
              (Stacks.Algebraization.idealPowerQuotientDrop (J.comap f) h F)).hom),
      ∀ (n : ℕ) (x : Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.cohomologyOverBase (Γ(Y, ⊤) : Type u)
          (toSpecGlobalSections f) 0 F),
        Stacks.IntertwinedFiltration.towerLimit.proj n
            (e (AdicCompletion.of _ _ x)) =
          (Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.cohomologyOverBaseMap (Γ(Y, ⊤) : Type u)
            (toSpecGlobalSections f) 0
            (cokernel.π (C := X.Modules)
              (Stacks.Algebraization.idealPowerMultiple (J.comap f) n F).ι)).hom x := by
  let : IsNoetherianRing (Γ(Y, ⊤) : Type u) :=
    IsLocallyNoetherian.component_noetherian ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top Y⟩
  rw [show J.comap f = Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.baseIdealSheaf (Γ(Y, ⊤) : Type u)
      (J.ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top Y⟩) (toSpecGlobalSections f) from
    (baseIdealSheaf_toSpecGlobalSections f J).symm]
  obtain ⟨e, he⟩ := Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.exists_formalFunctionsEquiv_of_02O8
    (Γ(Y, ⊤) : Type u) (toSpecGlobalSections f) (isProper_toSpecGlobalSections f)
    (J.ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top Y⟩) F
    (AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentAbelian.stacksIsCoherent_of_isCoherent ‹F.IsCoherent›) 0
    Stacks.FormalFunctions.isReesFinite_cohomologyIdealPowerSystem
  exact ⟨e, he⟩

/-- Naturality of `Stacks.Coherent.rightDerivedZeroSectionsEquiv`. -/
public lemma rightDerivedZeroSectionsEquiv_naturality {X Y : Scheme.{u}} [IsAffine Y]
    (f : X ⟶ Y) {N M : X.Modules} (φ : N ⟶ M)
    (x : Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.cohomologyOverBase (Γ(Y, ⊤) : Type u)
      (toSpecGlobalSections f) 0 N) :
    rightDerivedZeroSectionsEquiv f M
        ((Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.cohomologyOverBaseMap (Γ(Y, ⊤) : Type u)
          (toSpecGlobalSections f) 0 φ).hom x) =
      ((Stacks.Algebraization.affineSectionFunctor (⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top Y⟩ : Y.affineOpens)).map
        ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).map φ)).hom (rightDerivedZeroSectionsEquiv f N x) :=
  congrArg (fun k : ((Stacks.Cohomology.AffineBase.moduleGlobalSections X).rightDerived 0).obj N ⟶
      (Stacks.Cohomology.AffineBase.moduleGlobalSections X).obj M => k.hom x)
    ((Functor.rightDerivedZeroIsoSelf
      (Stacks.Cohomology.AffineBase.moduleGlobalSections X)).hom.naturality φ)

/-- The `n`-th term of the completion of `H` is the `(n+1)`-st term of the tower of ideal-power
quotients of `H`. -/
public def completionTermIso {X : Scheme.{u}} [IsLocallyNoetherian X] (I : X.IdealSheafData)
    (H : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.CoherentModules X.ringCatSheaf) (n : ℕ) :
    ((Stacks.Algebraization.completionFunctor X I).obj H).obj.obj (op n) ≅
      Stacks.Algebraization.idealPowerQuotient I (n + 1) H.obj :=
  eqToIso (Stacks.Algebraization.completionFunctor_obj X I H n)

/-- Under that identification the completion projection is the quotient projection. -/
public lemma completionProjection_comp_completionTermIso {X : Scheme.{u}}
    [IsLocallyNoetherian X] (I : X.IdealSheafData)
    (H : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.CoherentModules X.ringCatSheaf) (n : ℕ) :
    Stacks.Algebraization.completionProjection X I H n ≫ (completionTermIso I H n).hom =
      cokernel.π (C := X.Modules)
        (Stacks.Algebraization.idealPowerMultiple I (n + 1) H.obj).ι := by
  have h1 : eqToHom (Stacks.Algebraization.completionFunctor_obj X I H n).symm ≫
      eqToHom (Stacks.Algebraization.completionFunctor_obj X I H n) =
      𝟙 (Stacks.Algebraization.idealPowerQuotient I (n + 1) H.obj) := by
    rw [eqToHom_trans, eqToHom_refl]
  have h2 : Stacks.Algebraization.completionProjection X I H n ≫
        (completionTermIso I H n).hom =
      cokernel.π (C := X.Modules)
          (Stacks.Algebraization.idealPowerMultiple I (n + 1) H.obj).ι ≫
        (eqToHom (Stacks.Algebraization.completionFunctor_obj X I H n).symm ≫
          eqToHom (Stacks.Algebraization.completionFunctor_obj X I H n)) :=
    Category.assoc _ _ _
  rw [h2, h1]
  exact Category.comp_id _

/-- Under that identification the quotient projection is the completion projection. -/
public lemma cokernelπ_comp_completionTermIso_inv {X : Scheme.{u}} [IsLocallyNoetherian X]
    (I : X.IdealSheafData)
    (H : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.CoherentModules X.ringCatSheaf) (n : ℕ) :
    cokernel.π (C := X.Modules)
          (Stacks.Algebraization.idealPowerMultiple I (n + 1) H.obj).ι ≫
        (completionTermIso I H n).inv =
      Stacks.Algebraization.completionProjection X I H n :=
  (congrArg (fun k => k ≫ (completionTermIso I H n).inv)
      (completionProjection_comp_completionTermIso I H n)).symm.trans
    ((Category.assoc _ _ _).trans
      ((congrArg (fun k => Stacks.Algebraization.completionProjection X I H n ≫ k)
        (completionTermIso I H n).hom_inv_id).trans (Category.comp_id _)))

/-- The identification carries the transition maps of the completion to the exponent-lowering
maps of the ideal-power tower. -/
public lemma completionTermIso_naturality {X : Scheme.{u}} [IsLocallyNoetherian X]
    (I : X.IdealSheafData)
    (H : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.CoherentModules X.ringCatSheaf) {m n : ℕ}
    (h : m ≤ n) :
    ((Stacks.Algebraization.completionFunctor X I).obj H).obj.map (homOfLE h).op ≫
        (completionTermIso I H m).hom =
      (completionTermIso I H n).hom ≫
        Stacks.Algebraization.idealPowerQuotientDrop I (Nat.add_le_add_right h 1) H.obj := by
  have := Stacks.Algebraization.epi_completionProjection X I H n
  refine (cancel_epi (C := X.Modules)
    (Stacks.Algebraization.completionProjection X I H n)).1 ?_
  have hL : Stacks.Algebraization.completionProjection X I H n ≫
      (((Stacks.Algebraization.completionFunctor X I).obj H).obj.map (homOfLE h).op ≫
        (completionTermIso I H m).hom) =
      cokernel.π (C := X.Modules)
        (Stacks.Algebraization.idealPowerMultiple I (m + 1) H.obj).ι :=
    (Category.assoc _ _ _).symm.trans
      ((congrArg (fun k => k ≫ (completionTermIso I H m).hom)
        (Stacks.Algebraization.completionProjection_naturality I H (homOfLE h).op)).trans
        (completionProjection_comp_completionTermIso I H m))
  have hR : Stacks.Algebraization.completionProjection X I H n ≫
      ((completionTermIso I H n).hom ≫
        Stacks.Algebraization.idealPowerQuotientDrop I (Nat.add_le_add_right h 1) H.obj) =
      cokernel.π (C := X.Modules)
        (Stacks.Algebraization.idealPowerMultiple I (m + 1) H.obj).ι :=
    (Category.assoc _ _ _).symm.trans
      ((congrArg (fun k => k ≫
          Stacks.Algebraization.idealPowerQuotientDrop I (Nat.add_le_add_right h 1) H.obj)
        (completionProjection_comp_completionTermIso I H n)).trans
        (Stacks.Algebraization.idealPowerQuotientDrop_π I (Nat.add_le_add_right h 1) H.obj))
  exact hL.trans hR.symm

/-- The inverse form of `Stacks.Coherent.completionTermIso_naturality`. -/
public lemma completionTermIso_inv_naturality {X : Scheme.{u}} [IsLocallyNoetherian X]
    (I : X.IdealSheafData)
    (H : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.CoherentModules X.ringCatSheaf) {m n : ℕ}
    (h : m ≤ n) :
    (completionTermIso I H n).inv ≫
        ((Stacks.Algebraization.completionFunctor X I).obj H).obj.map (homOfLE h).op =
      Stacks.Algebraization.idealPowerQuotientDrop I (Nat.add_le_add_right h 1) H.obj ≫
        (completionTermIso I H m).inv := by
  rw [Iso.inv_comp_eq, ← Category.assoc, Iso.eq_comp_inv]
  exact completionTermIso_naturality I H h

/-- A functor into modules carries a factorisation `f ≫ g = h` to the corresponding identity of
linear maps. -/
private lemma map_hom_comp_apply {C : Type*} [Category C] {R : Type*} [Ring R]
    (S : C ⥤ ModuleCat R) {a b c : C} {f : a ⟶ b} {g : b ⟶ c} {h : a ⟶ c} (e : f ≫ g = h)
    (x : S.obj a) : (S.map g).hom ((S.map f).hom x) = (S.map h).hom x := by
  rw [← e, S.map_comp]
  rfl

/-- **The theorem on formal functions over an affine Noetherian base, as a statement about the
sections of the completion.** The `𝒥(Y)`-adic completion of `Γ(Y, f_*𝓕)` is the limit of the
sections of the direct images of the terms of the completion of `𝓕`, by the comparison assembled
from the projections. -/
public lemma exists_pushforwardCompletionSectionsEquiv
    {X Y : Scheme.{u}} [IsAffine Y] [IsNoetherian Y] (f : X ⟶ Y) [IsProper f]
    (J : Y.IdealSheafData) (F : X.Modules) [F.IsCoherent] :
    letI : IsLocallyNoetherian X := LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian f
    ∃ e : AdicCompletion (J.ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top Y⟩)
            ((Stacks.Algebraization.affineSectionFunctor
                (⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top Y⟩ : Y.affineOpens)).obj
              ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).obj F)) ≃ₗ[Γ(Y, ⊤)]
          (limit (((Stacks.Algebraization.completionFunctor X (J.comap f)).obj
              ⟨F, inferInstance⟩).obj ⋙ Scheme.Modules.pushforward f ⋙
              Stacks.Algebraization.affineSectionFunctor
                (⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top Y⟩ : Y.affineOpens)) : ModuleCat Γ(Y, ⊤)),
      ∀ (n : ℕ) (x : (Stacks.Algebraization.affineSectionFunctor
            (⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top Y⟩ : Y.affineOpens)).obj
          ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).obj F)),
        (limit.π (((Stacks.Algebraization.completionFunctor X (J.comap f)).obj
              ⟨F, inferInstance⟩).obj ⋙ Scheme.Modules.pushforward f ⋙
            Stacks.Algebraization.affineSectionFunctor
              (⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top Y⟩ : Y.affineOpens)) (op n)).hom
            (e (AdicCompletion.of _ _ x)) =
          ((Stacks.Algebraization.affineSectionFunctor
              (⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top Y⟩ : Y.affineOpens)).map
            ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).map
              (Stacks.Algebraization.completionProjection X (J.comap f)
                ⟨F, inferInstance⟩ n))).hom x := by
  let : IsLocallyNoetherian X := LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian f
  obtain ⟨e₀, he₀⟩ := exists_cohomologyTowerEquiv f J F
  have hT : IsTowerTransitive (A := (Γ(Y, ⊤) : Type u))
      (P := fun n => Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.cohomologyOverBase
        (Γ(Y, ⊤) : Type u) (toSpecGlobalSections f) 0
        (Stacks.Algebraization.idealPowerQuotient (J.comap f) n F))
      (fun _ _ h => (Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.cohomologyOverBaseMap
        (Γ(Y, ⊤) : Type u) (toSpecGlobalSections f) 0
        (Stacks.Algebraization.idealPowerQuotientDrop (J.comap f) h F)).hom) := by
    intro m n k h h' x
    have hcomp : Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.cohomologyOverBaseMap (Γ(Y, ⊤) : Type u)
            (toSpecGlobalSections f) 0
            (Stacks.Algebraization.idealPowerQuotientDrop (J.comap f) h' F) ≫
          Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.cohomologyOverBaseMap (Γ(Y, ⊤) : Type u)
            (toSpecGlobalSections f) 0
            (Stacks.Algebraization.idealPowerQuotientDrop (J.comap f) h F) =
        Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.cohomologyOverBaseMap (Γ(Y, ⊤) : Type u)
          (toSpecGlobalSections f) 0
          (Stacks.Algebraization.idealPowerQuotientDrop (J.comap f) (h.trans h') F) := by
      rw [← idealPowerQuotientDrop_comp (J.comap f) F h h']
      simp only [Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.cohomologyOverBaseMap, Functor.map_comp]
    exact congrArg (fun k : Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.cohomologyOverBase
      (Γ(Y, ⊤) : Type u) (toSpecGlobalSections f) 0
        (Stacks.Algebraization.idealPowerQuotient (J.comap f) k F) ⟶ _ => k.hom x) hcomp
  have hθ : IsShiftCompatible (A := (Γ(Y, ⊤) : Type u))
      (P := fun n => Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.cohomologyOverBase
        (Γ(Y, ⊤) : Type u) (toSpecGlobalSections f) 0
        (Stacks.Algebraization.idealPowerQuotient (J.comap f) n F))
      (fun _ _ h => (Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.cohomologyOverBaseMap
        (Γ(Y, ⊤) : Type u) (toSpecGlobalSections f) 0
        (Stacks.Algebraization.idealPowerQuotientDrop (J.comap f) h F)).hom)
      ((((Stacks.Algebraization.completionFunctor X (J.comap f)).obj
          ⟨F, inferInstance⟩).obj ⋙ Scheme.Modules.pushforward f ⋙
        Stacks.Algebraization.affineSectionFunctor (⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top Y⟩ : Y.affineOpens)))
      (fun n => (rightDerivedZeroSectionsEquiv f
          (Stacks.Algebraization.idealPowerQuotient (J.comap f) (n + 1) F)).trans
        ((Stacks.Algebraization.affineSectionFunctor
            (⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top Y⟩ : Y.affineOpens)).mapIso
          ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).mapIso
            (completionTermIso (J.comap f) ⟨F, inferInstance⟩ n).symm)).toLinearEquiv) := by
    intro m n h x
    have hnat := rightDerivedZeroSectionsEquiv_naturality f
      (Stacks.Algebraization.idealPowerQuotientDrop (J.comap f)
        (Nat.add_le_add_right h 1) F) x
    let S := Scheme.Modules.pushforward f ⋙ Stacks.Algebraization.affineSectionFunctor
      (⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top Y⟩ : Y.affineOpens)
    exact (map_hom_comp_apply S
      (completionTermIso_inv_naturality (J.comap f) ⟨F, inferInstance⟩ h) _).trans
      ((map_hom_comp_apply S rfl _).symm.trans (congrArg _ hnat.symm))
  have hofx : ∀ x : (Stacks.Algebraization.affineSectionFunctor
        (⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top Y⟩ : Y.affineOpens)).obj ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).obj F),
      (((AdicCompletion.congr (J.ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top Y⟩)
            (rightDerivedZeroSectionsEquiv f F)).restrictScalars
          (Γ(Y, ⊤) : Type u)).symm) (AdicCompletion.of _ _ x) =
        AdicCompletion.of _ _ ((rightDerivedZeroSectionsEquiv f F).symm x) := fun _ => rfl
  refine ⟨(((AdicCompletion.congr (J.ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top Y⟩)
      (rightDerivedZeroSectionsEquiv f F)).restrictScalars
      (Γ(Y, ⊤) : Type u)).symm.trans e₀).trans (towerEquivLimitShift hT hθ), fun n x => ?_⟩
  rw [LinearEquiv.trans_apply, LinearEquiv.trans_apply, hofx x,
    limit_π_towerEquivLimitShift hT hθ n, he₀ (n + 1)]
  refine (congrArg (fun z => ((Stacks.Algebraization.affineSectionFunctor
    (⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top Y⟩ : Y.affineOpens)).map ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).map
      (completionTermIso (J.comap f) ⟨F, inferInstance⟩ n).inv)).hom z)
    (rightDerivedZeroSectionsEquiv_naturality f
      (cokernel.π (C := X.Modules)
        (Stacks.Algebraization.idealPowerMultiple (J.comap f) (n + 1) F).ι)
      ((rightDerivedZeroSectionsEquiv f F).symm x))).trans ?_
  have hback : rightDerivedZeroSectionsEquiv f F
      ((rightDerivedZeroSectionsEquiv f F).symm x) = x :=
    (rightDerivedZeroSectionsEquiv f F).apply_symm_apply x
  rw [hback]
  exact map_hom_comp_apply (Scheme.Modules.pushforward f ⋙
    Stacks.Algebraization.affineSectionFunctor (⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top Y⟩ : Y.affineOpens))
    (cokernelπ_comp_completionTermIso_inv (J.comap f) ⟨F, inferInstance⟩ n) x

/-- **The comparison map of Stacks 088B is an isomorphism on sections over an affine Noetherian
base.** Only the computation rule of the comparison against the completion projections is used,
so the statement applies to the comparison morphism of
`Stacks.Coherent.pushforwardCompletionComparison`. -/
public lemma isIso_limMap_affineSections_of_completionProjection_comp
    {X Y : Scheme.{u}} [IsAffine Y] [IsNoetherian Y] (f : X ⟶ Y) [IsProper f]
    (J : Y.IdealSheafData) (F : X.Modules) [F.IsCoherent] :
    letI : IsLocallyNoetherian X := LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian f
    letI : ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).obj F).IsCoherent :=
      AlgebraicGeometry.ProperCoherenceWitness.isCoherent_pushforward f F
    ∀ c : ((Stacks.Algebraization.completionFunctor Y J).obj
          ⟨(Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).obj F, inferInstance⟩).obj ⟶
        ((Stacks.Algebraization.completionFunctor X (J.comap f)).obj ⟨F, inferInstance⟩).obj ⋙
          Scheme.Modules.pushforward f,
      (∀ n : ℕ, Stacks.Algebraization.completionProjection Y J
            ⟨(Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).obj F, inferInstance⟩ n ≫ c.app (op n) =
          (Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).map
            (Stacks.Algebraization.completionProjection X (J.comap f) ⟨F, inferInstance⟩ n)) →
      IsIso (limMap (Functor.whiskerRight c
        (Stacks.Algebraization.affineSectionFunctor
          (⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top Y⟩ : Y.affineOpens)))) := by
  let : IsLocallyNoetherian X := LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian f
  let : ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).obj F).IsCoherent :=
    AlgebraicGeometry.ProperCoherenceWitness.isCoherent_pushforward f F
  intro c hc
  let : IsNoetherianRing (Γ(Y, ⊤) : Type u) :=
    IsLocallyNoetherian.component_noetherian ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top Y⟩
  have : PreservesLimit (((Stacks.Algebraization.completionFunctor Y J).obj
      ⟨(Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).obj F, inferInstance⟩).obj)
      (Stacks.Algebraization.affineSectionFunctor
        (⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top Y⟩ : Y.affineOpens)) :=
    Stacks.Algebraization.affineSectionFunctor_preservesLimit _ _
  obtain ⟨eQ, heQ⟩ := exists_pushforwardCompletionSectionsEquiv f J F
  obtain ⟨eP, hePπ⟩ : ∃ eP : AdicCompletion (J.ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top Y⟩)
        ((Stacks.Algebraization.affineSectionFunctor
            (⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top Y⟩ : Y.affineOpens)).obj
          ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).obj F)) ≃ₗ[Γ(Y, ⊤)]
      (limit (((Stacks.Algebraization.completionFunctor Y J).obj
          ⟨(Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).obj F, inferInstance⟩).obj ⋙
        Stacks.Algebraization.affineSectionFunctor
          (⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top Y⟩ : Y.affineOpens)) : ModuleCat Γ(Y, ⊤)),
      ∀ (k : ℕᵒᵖ) (s : (Stacks.Algebraization.affineSectionFunctor
          (⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top Y⟩ : Y.affineOpens)).obj
        ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).obj F)),
        (limit.π (((Stacks.Algebraization.completionFunctor Y J).obj
            ⟨(Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).obj F, inferInstance⟩).obj ⋙
          Stacks.Algebraization.affineSectionFunctor
            (⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top Y⟩ : Y.affineOpens)) k).hom
            (eP (AdicCompletion.of _ _ s)) =
          ((Stacks.Algebraization.affineSectionFunctor
              (⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top Y⟩ : Y.affineOpens)).map
            (Stacks.Algebraization.completionProjection Y J
              ⟨(Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).obj F, inferInstance⟩ k.unop)).hom s := by
    refine ⟨(Stacks.Algebraization.completionSectionsEquiv Y J
        ⟨(Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).obj F, inferInstance⟩
        (⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top Y⟩ : Y.affineOpens)).trans
      (preservesLimitIso (Stacks.Algebraization.affineSectionFunctor
          (⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top Y⟩ : Y.affineOpens))
        (((Stacks.Algebraization.completionFunctor Y J).obj
          ⟨(Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).obj F, inferInstance⟩).obj)).toLinearEquiv,
      fun k s => ?_⟩
    refine (ConcreteCategory.congr_hom (preservesLimitIso_hom_π
      (Stacks.Algebraization.affineSectionFunctor (⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top Y⟩ : Y.affineOpens))
      (((Stacks.Algebraization.completionFunctor Y J).obj
        ⟨(Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).obj F, inferInstance⟩).obj) k) _).trans ?_
    refine (congrArg _ (Stacks.Algebraization.completionSectionsEquiv_of Y J
      ⟨(Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).obj F, inferInstance⟩
      (⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top Y⟩ : Y.affineOpens) s)).trans ?_
    exact map_hom_comp_apply _ (Stacks.Algebraization.completionToLimit_projection Y J
      ⟨(Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).obj F, inferInstance⟩ k) s
  refine isIso_of_adicCompletion_equiv (J.ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top Y⟩)
    (IsNoetherian.noetherian _) eP eQ _ fun s => ?_
  refine Concrete.limit_ext _ _ _ fun k => ?_
  refine (ConcreteCategory.congr_hom (limMap_π (Functor.whiskerRight c
    (Stacks.Algebraization.affineSectionFunctor
      (⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top Y⟩ : Y.affineOpens))) k) _).trans ?_
  refine (congrArg _ (hePπ k s)).trans ?_
  exact (map_hom_comp_apply _ (hc k.unop) s).trans (heQ k.unop s).symm


/-- **The theorem on formal functions in the form Stacks 088B needs, over an affine Noetherian
base.** The comparison `(f_*𝓕)^ ⟶ f_*(𝓕^)` of
`Stacks.Coherent.pushforwardCompletionComparison` becomes an isomorphism after taking the limit
of the global sections. -/
public theorem isIso_limMap_affineSections_pushforwardCompletionComparison
    {X Y : Scheme.{u}} [IsAffine Y] [IsNoetherian Y] (f : X ⟶ Y) [IsProper f]
    (J : Y.IdealSheafData) (F : X.Modules) [F.IsCoherent] :
    letI : IsLocallyNoetherian X := LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian f
    letI : ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).obj F).IsCoherent :=
      AlgebraicGeometry.ProperCoherenceWitness.isCoherent_pushforward f F
    IsIso (limMap (Functor.whiskerRight (pushforwardCompletionComparison f J F)
      (Stacks.Algebraization.affineSectionFunctor
        (⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top Y⟩ : Y.affineOpens)))) := by
  let : IsLocallyNoetherian X := LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian f
  let : ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).obj F).IsCoherent :=
    AlgebraicGeometry.ProperCoherenceWitness.isCoherent_pushforward f F
  exact isIso_limMap_affineSections_of_completionProjection_comp f J F
    (pushforwardCompletionComparison f J F) (pushforwardCompletionComponent_π f J F)

end Stacks.Coherent

